`h` is declared here; Res is nocopy, so it has a single owner
captured here by a closure that is stored in `reader`
note: a nocopy value can only be borrowed by a lambda passed directly as a call argument, or by a spawn awaited in the same block
help: to share it with a closure that is stored, returned or outlives this block, make it reference counted:
    val h = rc open_res("data.txt")
the closure then holds its own reference, and the value is dropped once, when the last holder is gone
